    "releaseNotes": "2.2.1 : pr\u00e9requis Astra Framework [3.0.0, 5.0.0), compatible avec le framework 4.1.0. Plage \u00e9largie aux frameworks 4.x ; contenu et code inchang\u00e9s. 2.2.0: framework 3.0.0 (audio and feedback engines extracted into the Echo and Pulse packages). The Astra bridge follows the extraction: feedback players, requests and targets come from the Pulse package (com.misterpxl.pulse, namespace Astra.Pulse); rules and content unchanged. Requires the package com.misterpxl.pulse [1.0.0, 2.0.0) and astra-framework [3.0.0, 4.0.0); on a 2.x framework the import does not compile. 2.1.0: Tactics Studio chapter editor (Tools/Astra/Tactics/Studio): library, canvas with seven modes and registry brushes, Issues from ChapterValidation, Preview tab (danger zone, move range, forecast, AI dry run, seed), Play from the studio with live state, chapter text import with a reviewed diff and export, scene-view Tactics Stage Paint tool, Aegis chapter and ruleset rules; unit placements gain DeploySlot and an inventory override; chapter names and objectives resolve through the label table. The old Map editor window is removed.",
